<!--
  TerraHawk Scout v2 robot description - GENERATED by urdf/gen_description.py, do not hand-edit.
  Params: out/robot_params.json  (version v2-r3)

  DESIGN LEDGER
  - Frames: REP-103. base_footprint = ground plane at the centre of rotation (midpoint of the
    front and rear axles, on the centreline). +X forward (Elegoo servo / Dead Plate end), +Y left, +Z up.
  - Units: metres, kilograms, radians. Params file is already in this frame (no transform).
  - base_link: fixed above base_footprint at mean axle height z=0.0325 m. Its inertial lumps every
    rigid chassis part in the params file (100 links, 0.898 kg, parallel-axis theorem in sim/scout_params.py).
  - Wheels: 4 continuous joints wheel_<fl|fr|rl|rr>_joint, axis +Y on every wheel, so a positive
    joint velocity rolls the robot forward on BOTH sides (no mirrored sign). Radius 0.0325 m,
    width 0.026 m, track 0.124 m, wheelbase 0.08 m.
    Wheel visual/collision cylinder is rotated rpy=(pi/2,0,0) so its axis lies along the joint axis.
  - Limits: effort = stall torque 0.1648 N m, velocity = no-load 22.56 rad/s:
    Hiwonder TT Hall-encoder 1:42 at the 8.4 V PWM average-voltage cap (sim/motor_profiles.json hiwonder_1_42_8v4;
    listing values, unverified - bench-test on arrival).
  - Sensors (fixed joints from base_link): laser_link at the scan plane (z=0.148905 above ground),
    camera_link (X forward body convention, pitched 15 deg down = rpy 0 +0.2618 0) + camera_optical_link (REP-103
    optical: z forward, x right, y down; rpy = -pi/2 0 -pi/2), imu_link (MPU-6050 die, GY-521 hung chip-down: roll pi),
    ultrasonic_link (X = sensing direction). RPLIDAR C1 native angles are clockwise; sllidar_ros2 converts.
  - Payload: the CAD keep-out cylinder (D75 x 80 mm, 300 g) at x = -50 mm; xacro arg payload:=true, and the expanded
    scout_payload.urdf.
  - Collision: boxes from each params link bbox (plates, motors, boards, LiDAR), cylinders for wheels. Cable routes
    (cable_*) are in the inertial lump only.
  - Assumptions: see the params file's mass_source fields (measured / datasheet / assumed / cad-volume x density).
-->
